# emem.eio — this file is the whole site.
# One statement per line: <verb> <args>. `<<` opens a block, `>>` closes it.
# src/eio.mjs reads it. It turns `hero` `in` `give` `check` `foot` into the page
# and runs `flow` step by step. Braces {x} are filled from the run.

title   emem
hero    One link. Every AI reads the same source.

in      drop  Drop a file, paste text, or paste a link
accept  pdf docx txt md csv json html htm xml log  js ts py rs go java c h css yaml toml sql
limit   2000000

# the path from anything to a link
flow    take  -> text  -> sign  -> put  -> link
# the path from a link back to proof
open    fetch -> hash  -> match

give    copy   Copy for AI       {prompt}
give    copy   Copy with text    {prompt_text}
give    go     ChatGPT           https://chatgpt.com/?q={prompt}
give    go     Claude            https://claude.ai/new?q={prompt}

check   Paste the AI's answer. Every "quote" is checked against the source.

prompt <<
Source: {url}
Read the source before you answer. When you rely on it, quote it word for word in "double quotes". If the source does not say it, say that.
emem · {cid} · the file name is the hash of its bytes
>>

prompt_text <<
Source: {url}
Answer from the source below. When you rely on it, quote it word for word in "double quotes". If the source does not say it, say that.
emem · {cid}
----- source -----
{text}
----- end -----
>>

foot    Public. Anyone with the link can read it. Signed by this browser · {key}
